  "question": {
    "text": "An inductor <math> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.03</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>H</mtext></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </math> and a resistor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>k&#937;</mtext><mo>)</mo></math> are connected in series to a battery of <math> <mn>15</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>V</mtext> </math> E.M.F. in a circuit shown below. The key <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> has been kept closed for a long time. Then at <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is opened and key <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is closed simultaneously. At <math> <mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>ms</mtext> </math> , the current in the circuit will be : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Take</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0159_4e4e9817e05b.jpg\" style=\"width: 208px; height: 167px;\" />"
  },
